\begin{readerbox}{Observed local execution, 20 October 2026}
At the original CP12 checkpoint, the author-run shared suite passed \textbf{428 tests} (7 acceptance, 421 regression), including the 24 new incident tests. These historical counts precede the later chapter additions. The CP12 validator passed \textbf{53/53 assertions}, including 9 negative scenarios; the current-source rehearsal passed 31/31 checks and recovery passed 40/40. The inherited Chapters~1--9, 10 and 11 workflow validators passed 53/53, 49/49 and 37/37 assertions respectively. These are separate scopes, not an additive test total. Delivered sources and both original incident ledgers remained unchanged. Detailed evidence is retained under \path{editorial/verification/chapter12/VALIDATION_AGGREGATE.json}. Local restoration passed; owner reconciliation, independent human review and a live operational transfer trial remain pending. No production recovery, incident closure or release is claimed.
\end{readerbox}

\begin{readerbox}{Observed local execution, 20 October 2026}
At the original CP14 checkpoint, the author-run shared suite passed \textbf{482 tests} (7 acceptance, 475 regression), including the 28 new measurement tests. The following counts describe that retained run, not a new run triggered by reading this edition. All six cumulative workflow validators passed. The current measurement rehearsal passed 33/33 checks and its gate 34/34; these are distinct scopes. Six command executions covered five attempts and one protected synthetic accepted handoff, with the scenario total reconciled to \textbf{EUR~37.64}. Evidence is retained under \path{editorial/verification/chapter14/VALIDATION_AGGREGATE.json}. Source files were unchanged by validation. Recorded durations describe local process intervals, not performance benchmarks. Actual human effort, billing and acceptance remain unmeasured; the field pilot, live comparison and independent human reviewer confirmation remain pending.
\end{readerbox}

\begin{readerbox}{Observed local execution, 20 October 2026}
At the original CP13 checkpoint, the author-run shared suite passed \textbf{454 tests} (7 acceptance, 447 regression), including the 26 new learning tests. These historical counts precede the Chapter~14 additions. All five cumulative workflow validators passed. The CP13 validator passed \textbf{54/54 assertions}, including 8 negative scenarios; the current transfer rehearsal passed 37/37 checks and the learning gate passed 24/24. These are separate scopes, not an additive test total. Synthetic calibration exercised phase ordering, raw scores and separate adjudication. The starter and protected unsafe control were rejected as intended. Detailed evidence, including the initial harness failure and corrected rerun, is retained under \path{editorial/verification/chapter13/VALIDATION_AGGREGATE.json}. Delivered source remained unchanged by validation. The real delayed human trial, independent human scoring, rubric validation and human reviewer confirmation remain pending; no learning gain or new operational authority is claimed.
\end{readerbox}
